<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charlotte Stanley, Countess of Derby</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1599">1599</a>–<a href="/years/1664">1664</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Charlotte de La Trémoille</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charlotte Stanley, Countess of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derby">Derby</a>, born Charlotte de La Trémoille, was a French Huguenot noblewoman who married James Stanley, later 7th <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/earl-of-derby">Earl of Derby</a>, in 1626. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-civil-war">English Civil War</a> she held Lathom House against a parliamentary siege in 1644. She later defended the Isle of Man, which was surrendered to Parliament in 1651, shortly after her husband's execution.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charlotte-stanley-countess-of-derby.jpg" alt="Charlotte Stanley, Countess of Derby" width="320" height="362" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to Michiel Jansz. van Mierevelt · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charlotte_de_la_Tr%C3%A9mo%C3%AFlle_(1599%E2%80%931664),_Lady_Strange,_Later_Countess_of_Derby.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
